Antilles wrote:
> I have a related question.  Aside from what you should put in your
> stash, I'd like to know where to put it.

Ideally, if I have the Eye it goes in Sokoban (bottom level).  If not,
it goes on a level with an altar and a closet (for changing/enchanting
armor, etc), or a coaligned temple (for the same).  Early on or if I
haven't found an altar, it can go anywhere (maybe a level with a
general store for price-id).

In the early game the "stash" is often just dropping things next to the
downstairs (hopefully in a chest/box) before going down.  Later on
it'll be a box with Elbereth permanently engraved under it, and I'll go
grab all the earlier stashes and consolidate them into one main stash.

Early on you don't have to go _too_ far to get to the stash if it's in
the main branch.  Later on, use levelport or the Eye to get to/from it.
 You shouldn't have to return all that often anyway (usually 1-2 times
after I enter Gehennom; once just before waking Rodney to get all my
ascension run stuff together and do alchemy and other prep work, and
sometimes once to drop off loot if I'm finding a lot of stuff that I
feel is worth keeping)



